WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:02.660
I come in today with my mindset

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:03.980
all on doing one thing.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.420
And now it's complete 180, we're doing something else.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.720
Not only! Are we doing something completely different, we have to do it in a really really short amount of time.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.340
We need it to be cool.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.140
We need it to be special.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.640
Jake pitched Audible on this shadow idea.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.500
Which, I don't think he really had an idea. (laugh)

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.020
So, we're shooting on Wednesday, which is two days from now.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.360
And like a day or two for shooting.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.440
A day or two of editing.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.440
And then, a week of effects. And we chose an effects heavy video.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:27.980
Would you be shooting this?

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.220
No, because I have three videos to make this week.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.320
Okay, so who would shoot it?

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.640
Hey Niko

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:52.400
What's up

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.600
What's a set piece?

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:01.640
Set piece is a moment of coolness, a little self-contained spectacle bit that

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:05.520
makes you go "Ooh." Basically it's an after effects project file.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.740
Fifty-two times twelve. Last year I blocked almost two thousand phone numbers from my phone

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:18.620
I get about five... six phone calls a day from telemarketers

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.760
Every time they call, I don't answer and then I block the phone number instantly

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.880
The next day I get another four to five phone calls from telemarketers

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.300
from a whole new set of phone numbers and then I have to do it again

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.320
And then the next day and the next...

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.680
The only day they do not call is Sunday.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.440
Always after 9 and before 10 PM

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.800
It's really annoying because I have a FitBit

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.340
and my arm will just vibrate every time telemarketers call.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.940
This has been going on since last January, so 2016.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:51.000
I may have a solution to permanently get all the telemarketers to stop calling me

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.940
We have a brand integration for Audible

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.980
You guys have seen a couple Audible integrations in the Sam and Niko channel

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.440
which Wren has graciously recommended some great books to you guys.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:01.560
Wren: I LOVE BOOKS!

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.900
I love books... They're great

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.280
But this time they've actually agreed to do an integration on the Corridor channel

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.640
The downside is we have to turn around a video idea really quickly now

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.520
'Cause they want the integration to come out by April 30th

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:20.520
So we've got to write an idea and get it made and get it out there before the deadline hits

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.300
otherwise we lose the integration.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.800
Except you guys are gonna be at NAB

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.800
Or at flight fest

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.560
So we have to make a video before NAB?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.300
Jake pitched Audible on this shadow idea

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.360
which I don't think he really had an idea...

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.560
I think he was just like "Shadows. What if?"

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.960
This is a spiritual successor to brush with death, to paper cuts

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.920
It's like there's a very cool, just like perspective theme to it, right?

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.020
The idea of projections.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.520
We spent like two weeks last year working on some shadow video just like this

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.520
and it went nowhere.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.440
so we're revisiting it again this year.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.500
Yeah... We need an outline by the end of the day

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.180
I would say it would be up to you to direct the piece

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.180
in terms of like everything leading up to when shadows start to play.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.660
Really just focusing on the mood, the setups, the pay offs

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.600
And then I'd let Wren handle the visuals

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.940
So I'm that we do something way scarier

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.100
There's two guys. Like they're breaking into a property.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.980
They kind of split up. 'Cause like this one guy sees that there's this light on this...

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:29.120
Creature that's also a shadow leans out of the darkness and encroaches on him.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.500
This shadow creature if it grabs this guy it affects him in real life

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.380
So like maybe it reaches out and grabs a backpack

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.060
And so you can realize if this shadow creature touches your shadow, it affects you for real

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.480
[Pantomimes creature] Like the shadow just... to that guy's shadow. And then real life

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.740
Like stabs him through just "Gyaaah"

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.680
Yeah then real life, like you see the guy like blackness appears in his chest...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.200
And like sucks into him

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.880
Actually yeah, so what if it starts as black but then slowly becomes transparent

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.040
But because the back is also kinda dark and black it doesn't feel transparent right away

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.320
until he's completely gone. You realize you're just staring at nothing.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:01.820
Yeah

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.600
Now we've set the stakes. We know that if you get hit by the shadow creature

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.480
you get turned into a shadow.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.140
...so now, his friend comes into the room.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:13.640
I'm going to register my cell phone on the Do Not Call Registry from the FTC

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.460
It's the grumpy people list. Go to donotcall.gov

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.260
Do Not Call Registry does not expire. But what I was Googling it said it takes

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.900
about thirty one days to enact.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:30.340
Even if I do this, I still have to block 162 phone calls by the end of this month.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.480
Dude... You loving those chips?

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.780
Dude where'd those chips come from, son?

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:38.580
Chip fairy.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.940
The chip fairy?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.060
You literally can't stop once you eat one.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.560
Dude these look really hot, like spicy hot.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.260
You are covered in sweat!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.960
It's real dude!

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.660
Gotta keep eating them man or else you just shut down.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.500
Like once you start eating these things, you just hav-- you can't stop.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:07.500
'Cause your body will just shut down and like... you start sweating... It's like... Oof...

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.120
Don't judge me!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:09.620
Oh no!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.800
Maybe he grabs like a two by four and like sets it up, projects on the wall

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.540
so the thing can't get through the wall.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.480
The light switch on the other side of the room

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:21.920
"It's always called the thing that the characters on the screen worry about

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.580
but the audience don't care."

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.480
And all the light are on the ceiling

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.860
He ascertains that he can turn on that light switch he'll turn on all the lights in the room

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.860
thereby destroying the shadows

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.280
So he needs to get to that light switch.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.420
Trips on the cord!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.620
...That has this one light that's still on

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.580
and the whole room falls into darkness.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.660
And he's like "Oh shit"

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.260
Now he's completely surrounded by shadow and like you film like

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.660
a dude on a black background.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.600
You should like reach and like, it should be like--

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.200
Like he's trying to get closer but it's like getting closer and closer

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.860
You can actually see like the black hands like go on his face?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.360
The darkest hour of the character?

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:52.700
Yeah, the darkest hour. Exactly.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.940
I do like this idea.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.480
It sets up the stakes at the beginning.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:58.760
Cool visuals that probably won't actually be that hard to do

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.740
If we do it well.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.720
It's got a darkest hour where things get the worst they can possibly be

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.540
and they get solved right afterwards.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.480
...much bigger problem at the end.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.460
Who do you have play the dude?

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.620
Brett and I. Brett and I.

