just gotta actually write it.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.340
Tricky part here is now we have to come up with the specifics

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.660
We need to lay out exactly what happens.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.700
Yeah, I tweeted this a few days ago

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.340
but it's like literally the hardest thing I find to do here at work is

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.600
literally just coming up with ideas.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.340
Which is strange, I always thought you were a big ideas guy.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:19.080
I mean, I mean, yeah. But like... sure.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.620
But that is-- I consider coming up with a good idea worth doing is way more difficult

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:27.060
than any other visual effects, the production side. Those are all technically hard

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.760
this is very implicitly hard.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.700
You know there's like-- there's no way-- there's no tangible way to measure a good idea

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.480
until it's like done and uploaded.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.020
You know you can have an overall concept that's cool but then you'll be like

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:41.780
What's my idea for this line of dialogue?
 What's my idea for how I step into this scene?

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:43.360
How much tension do I want for this moment?

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.620
Yeah you've just gotta fall back to how you know how to structure a scene

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.260
You know our goal here is to get a cool script completely done today

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.320
